<td><p style="text-align: center" align="left"><font face="Times New Roman" size="7"><strong>HoloNet Transmission</strong></font><br> <font face="Times New Roman" size="5"><em><small>review by Jeff Hansen</small></em></font><br><small>[click <a href="https://web.archive.org/web/20190202044410/http://decipher.com/starwars/cardlists/dagobah/dark/large/holonettransmission.html" target="Main">here</a> to view card]</small></p>


A Dark Side Used or Lost Interrupt with two dots and a destiny of 2, this hologram belongs in Hunt Down decks. As a Used Interrupt, it cancels Transmission Terminated, the poison pill to Visage Of The Emperor. This alone is worth it! However, it's also quite attractive as a Lost Interrupt, searching your Used Pile and taking one Imperial or Visage Of The Emperor into hand, then reshuffling. If you know that Vader, Tarkin, or Mara is in your Used Pile; you can grab the one you need! If you're stocking more than four Vaders in your Hunt Down deck, by all means, replace at least one of the surplus Vaders with HoloNet Transmission! The destiny is better, the interrupt is much more versatile, and it can be grabbed with Masterful Move. HoloNet and Masterful work very slick in tandem, as it puts the low destiny in your hand while putting the high destiny back into your deck. This card was made for Hunt Down, as if Hunt Down wasn't powerful enough on its own... =)

